# Packaged Worker Env (NODE_PATH)

## Problem

Packaged Electron workers often live under `app.asar.unpacked/`. Bare
`require("puppeteer")` (and other EXTERNAL_DEPENDENCIES) resolve against that
tree and miss packages that only exist in `app.asar/node_modules`. On Windows
this becomes a recurring `MODULE_NOT_FOUND` crash after packaging.

## Required Pattern

**Every** `utilityProcess.fork(...)` and `spawn(process.execPath, ...)` call in
`src/` MUST pass env from `buildPackagedWorkerEnv`:

```typescript
import { buildPackagedWorkerEnv } from "@/utils/packagedWorkerPath";

// utilityProcess workers
utilityProcess.fork(workerPath, [], {
  stdio: "pipe",
  env: buildPackagedWorkerEnv({
    extraEnv: { WORKER_TYPE: "my-worker" },
  }),
});

// child_process.spawn workers that run Electron as Node
spawn(process.execPath, [workerPath], {
  stdio: ["pipe", "pipe", "pipe", "ipc"],
  env: buildPackagedWorkerEnv({
    runAsNode: true,
    extraEnv: {
      ELECTRON_APP_NAME: app.getName(),
      ELECTRON_USER_DATA_PATH: app.getPath("userData"),
    },
  }),
});
```

Also resolve worker paths with `resolvePackagedWorkerPath` so the `app.asar`
virtual path is preferred over `app.asar.unpacked` when both exist.

## Do Not

```typescript
// ❌ DON'T: hand-roll env without NODE_PATH
utilityProcess.fork(path, [], {
  env: { ...process.env, NODE_OPTIONS: "" },
});

// ❌ DON'T: invent a one-off getPackagedWorkerNodePath call site
// ❌ DON'T: add PackagedWorkerEnvGuard allowlist entries for new spawn sites
```

## Enforcement

- Unit tests: [packagedWorkerPath.test.ts](mdc:test/vitest/main/packagedWorkerPath.test.ts)
- Static gate: [PackagedWorkerEnvGuard.test.ts](mdc:test/vitest/main/PackagedWorkerEnvGuard.test.ts)
- Helper: [packagedWorkerPath.ts](mdc:src/utils/packagedWorkerPath.ts)

If the guard fails, wire the spawn through `buildPackagedWorkerEnv` — do not
weaken the gate.
